00:13:27.740 --> 00:13:28.960
Click Save.

00:13:28.960 --> 00:13:30.700
And when we save
that policy, it's

00:13:30.700 --> 00:13:33.310
actually going to be propagated
across the world within a very

00:13:33.310 --> 00:13:34.900
short period of time.

00:13:34.900 --> 00:13:37.990
All of the proxies across
Google's global network

00:13:37.990 --> 00:13:39.530
are immediately updated.

00:13:39.530 --> 00:13:42.820
So the next time any user tries
to access a protected resource,

00:13:42.820 --> 00:13:45.460
they're evaluated against
that new policy set.

00:13:45.460 --> 00:13:48.380
We mentioned continuous
authorization earlier,

00:13:48.380 --> 00:13:50.080
and this is a key part of that.

00:13:50.080 --> 00:13:52.730
Authorization is not
a one-time occurrence.

00:13:52.730 --> 00:13:54.730
So even if you
begin a new session,

00:13:54.730 --> 00:13:58.405
that doesn't mean you'll
have perpetual access.

00:13:58.405 --> 00:13:59.280
TANISHA RAI: Exactly.

00:13:59.280 --> 00:14:02.490
And for companies like Cymbal
that employ hourly and temp

00:14:02.490 --> 00:14:05.310
workers, the ability
to dynamically update

00:14:05.310 --> 00:14:07.410
access conditions is important.

00:14:07.410 --> 00:14:10.680
For instance, they could set
these policies so workers only

00:14:10.680 --> 00:14:13.830
access applications and
resources during their shift

00:14:13.830 --> 00:14:16.980
hours or working days,
or only allow access

00:14:16.980 --> 00:14:20.160
from specific geographies.

00:14:20.160 --> 00:14:22.470
They also may want to
require that devices

00:14:22.470 --> 00:14:25.440
have the most up-to-date
operating systems and security

00:14:25.440 --> 00:14:27.660
patches, so this is
an important condition

00:14:27.660 --> 00:14:30.330
to manage, especially for
all the contractors using

00:14:30.330 --> 00:14:31.650
their own devices.

00:14:31.650 --> 00:14:32.700
MARCO GENOVESE: Exactly.

